# Diagnostic codes without a case in diagnostics.cases (testing.md §3, BinderDiagnosticTests.EveryDiagnosticIsCovered).
# Scope: every E2xxx, W1xxx, W4xxx and Hxxxx code of DiagnosticCatalog (the codes opc itself reports outside the
# lexer, parser and driver error ranges). Each such code has a case or exactly one line here:
#   CODE  STATUS  reason
# STATUS is one of
#   reserved | retired        must match the "(reserved…)"/"(retired…)" note of its row in diagnostics.md
#   M2.2 … M2.6 | Phase3 | Phase4 | Phase8
#                             not reachable yet: the milestone/phase whose feature reports it; the task that makes it
#                             reachable moves it to diagnostics.cases (C-127 empties the M2.x part)
#   elsewhere <TestClass>     reported only by the driver or the toolchain, not by a source snippet; <TestClass> is a
#                             test class of FreexComp.Compiler.Tests that covers it
# A code with a case must not be listed; M2.1 is never a valid status.

E2001  M2.4  declaration mismatch of a forward class / method
E2006  M2.2  qualification of a non-record/unit name
E2007  M2.2  incomplete type (pointer forward, records)
E2008  reserved  LANG-516 makes this unused
E2015  M2.2  ^T forward reference (LANG-208)
E2016  M2.2  record/class/interface required (with, member access)
E2017  M2.2  array type required (indexing)
E2018  M2.2  pointer type required (dereference)
E2019  M2.2  too many indexes
E2022  M2.2  circular type definition
E2023  M2.2  result type restrictions (LANG-412)
E2031  M2.2  data structure too large
